 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2019-01-31",
   "text": "Merger Enforcement Improvement Act\n This bill modifies antitrust enforcement requirements regarding mergers. Specifically, the bill\n adjusts premerger notification filing fees; \n requires certain filers to report to the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) or to the relevant Assistant Attorney General on information that allows the government to assess the competitive impact of a merger; \n requires the FTC to study overlapping ownership or control by investors in certain markets; and \n requires the Government Accountability Office to assess the success of certain merger remedies and the impact of mergers and acquisitions on wages, employment, innovation, and new business formation."
  }
 ],
